+# raptor-hal, SigmaStar fork
+
+Upstream [gtxaspec/raptor-hal](https://github.com/gtxaspec/raptor-hal) plus a
+SigmaStar Infinity6C backend, for a port of Thingino to SigmaStar. It is branch
+`sigmastar` on top of gtxaspec main `9f09664`. The fork has no public remote:
+it is published as a patch series that applies with `git am` onto a bare
+checkout of `9f09664`.
+
+The rest of the Raptor stack (raptor, raptor-ipc, raptor-common, compy) runs
+**unmodified upstream at upstream Thingino's pins**. This is the one fork the
+port carries.
+
+## Base
+
+gtxaspec main `9f09664` (2026-10-30). It is 4 commits past upstream Thingino's
+`thingino-raptor-hal` pin `8897102`:
+
+- `38262ac` IVS move params in get/set_param;
+- `1d4f660` explicit QP deltas for CBR channels;
+- `f463040` no stream flush on T10/T20 IDR requests;
+- `9f09664` whole T41 manual white balance.
+
+Thingino's SigmaStar build pins this fork. Every other vendor keeps upstream
+Thingino's pin.
+
+## What is here, and where it came from
+
+In series order:
+
+| Commit | Content | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| `sigmastar-headers: vendor …` | `sigmastar-headers/`: reconstructed MI 2.x and MI 3.0 ABI headers, a plain directory (no submodule) | johnchia/sigmastar-headers `6fb6eec`, verbatim (see `sigmastar-headers/VENDORED.md`, `*/DERIVED.md`) |
+| `infinity6c: import …` | `src/infinity6c/`, `src/hal_symbols.h`, `src/caps_sigmastar.inc`, `src/hal_internal_sigmastar.h`, `mk/sigmastar.mk`; `src/hal_internal_hisilicon.h` is an `#error` stub | johnchia/raptor-hal `672f8b3` (branch `sigmastar`), verbatim |
+| `build: vendor hooks …` | `Makefile`, `src/hal_caps.c`, `src/hal_internal.h` (+87/−9) | John Chia's hook diff, applied to upstream |
+| `infinity6c: build against the upstream HAL interface` | the compat shim, `src/infinity6c/i6c_upstream_compat.{h,c}` | this fork |
+| `infinity6c: anti-flicker via FlickerEx manual lock` | `MI_ISP_AE_SetFlickerEx` manual lock, deferred to the first frame | this fork (GC8613 banding on the MC-A85) |
+| `infinity6c: map upstream raptor's 0..255 image knobs …` | the knob scale map and its host test `tests/t_knob_map_i6c.c` | this fork |
+| `FORK.md: …` | this file | this fork |
+| `infinity6c: report ae_luma on the 0..255 scale` | CUS3A's 10-bit `preAvgY` shifted to the 8-bit scale that ric's `night_luma` compares against | this fork |
+| `infinity6c: SCL->VENC ring depth from RSS_SCL_RING_DIV` | `i6c_pool_configure`: the SCL→VENC ring holds 1/N frame from `RSS_SCL_RING_DIV` (4 = a quarter, still the default; 2; 1) and logs the depth | this fork (a quarter frame let the scaler lap the main encoder on a YMF46D with a 720p sub) |
+| `infinity6c: opt-in AE max-shutter cap from RSS_AE_MAX_SHUTTER_US` | `i6c_isp_flush_ae_limit`: lowers the tuning's `maxShutterUs` through `MI_ISP_AE_Get/SetExposureLimit`, never below its minimum, after the first frame and every tuning reload; unset keeps the tuning's ceiling | this fork (holds the night frame rate at the cost of gain) |
+| `infinity6c: drop the dead H.265 rate-mode substitution` | removes `i6c_enc_note_rc_substitution` and `rc_substituted`, which could no longer fire once the UBR numbering replaced the remap | this fork |
+| `infinity6c: encoder I-frame cap, I/P QP bounds and delta, super frames` | `src/infinity6c/i6c_venc_rc.h` (the MI 3.0 `RcParam`, super-frame and RC-priority ABI, and the pure builder) and its host test `tests/t_venc_rc_i6c.c`; the ops `enc_set_qp_bounds`, `enc_set_qp_bounds_per_frame`, `enc_set_qp_ip_delta`, `enc_set_qp`, `enc_set_max_pic_size`, `enc_set/get_super_frame`; the six MI calls bind optionally | this fork (keyframes took nearly a second's budget at a 1 s GOP; the ops answered "not supported") |
+| `infinity6c: opt-in encoder statistics from RSS_VENC_STATS` | per-channel windows of the I-frame share, frame sizes and QP per frame type, plus the `RcParam` read back | this fork (the measurement for the I-frame cap) |
+
+## How the upstream interface is bridged
+
+John Chia's backend was written against his own fork's `include/raptor_hal.h`,
+which adds interface items upstream lacks. `src/infinity6c/i6c_upstream_compat.h`
+detects upstream by the absence of `RSS_ISP_AUTO` and defines
+`I6C_UPSTREAM_HAL_IFACE`. Under it:
+
+- **Getter types:** six ISP getters are published with upstream's `uint8_t *`
+  signature.
+- **Dropped items:** the knob-caps op and the green WB gain are left out, and
+  the sensor mode is forced to auto.
+- **The knob scale map** translates raptor's 0..255 / 128-default scale to each
+  module's native units (the header explains why and how).
+
+If upstream ever defines `RSS_ISP_AUTO` itself, the shim switches off. Check
+that the interfaces then agree before relying on it. The shim would go away if
+the backend moved to the current interface.
+
+## Build and test
+
+```bash
+make PLATFORM=INFINITY6C SOC_MODEL=ssc378de \
+     CROSS_COMPILE=<thingino host>/bin/arm-thingino-linux-uclibcgnueabihf-
+for t in tests/t_*_i6c.c; do
+  cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Iinclude -Isrc/infinity6c -o /tmp/t $t && /tmp/t
+done
+```
+
+The build needs only libc headers: MI is reached through `dlopen` at run time.
+On base `9f09664` (2026-11-06) both host tests pass, and Thingino's SigmaStar
+camera builds cross-compile the fork with GCC 16 uClibc, with and without
+`DEBUG=1`.
+
+## Structure for more families
+
+Everything is keyed by vendor and family, so 6E/6B0 (or HiSilicon) slot in
+without restructuring:
+
+- **Vendor fragment:** `mk/<vendor>.mk` (the Makefile `-include`s it).
+- **One backend directory per family:** `src/infinity6c/` now; John Chia's
+  `src/star/` (MI 2.x: Infinity6E/6B0) when wanted. `mk/sigmastar.mk` already
+  routes it.
+- **Headers per family:** `sigmastar-headers/<family>/`, with `infinity6e/`
+  already present.
+- **Platform chain:** `src/hal_internal_<vendor>.h`, one link per vendor.
+
+A `star` import needs its own compat pass, the same way `infinity6c` did.
+
+## Maintenance
+
+- **Rebase onto a newer gtxaspec:** branch a backup first, then
+  `git fetch upstream` and `git rebase --onto <new base> 9f09664 sigmastar`
+  (best the pin upstream Thingino moves to). Conflicts, if any, are in the
+  three hook files. Then rebuild, run the host test, and grep
+  `include/raptor_hal.h` for new or changed ISP ops the shim must cover.
+- **Refresh John Chia's backend:** fetch
+  [johnchia/raptor-hal](https://github.com/johnchia/raptor-hal) (branch
+  `sigmastar`), then
+  `git diff 672f8b3 <new> -- src/infinity6c mk/sigmastar.mk src/caps_sigmastar.inc src/hal_internal_sigmastar.h src/hal_symbols.h`,
+  apply it, and rebuild: a new fork-only interface use shows up as a compile
+  error.
+- **Refresh the headers:** re-copy `sigmastar-headers/` from
+  [johnchia/sigmastar-headers](https://github.com/johnchia/sigmastar-headers) at
+  a newer commit, keeping `VENDORED.md` current. Never edit them in place.
+- **Bump the firmware pin** after any change here that the build uses: the
+  SigmaStar branch of Thingino's `package/thingino-raptor-hal/thingino-raptor-hal.mk`
+  names the commit.
